- Anyone may use the application free of charge on the site where it is published, including for personal practice and for classes or lessons.
- The source code is publicly viewable but is not open source. Copying, modifying, redistributing or selling the source code or text, or publishing another application or service based on this application, requires permission from the copyright holder.
- Third-party works bundled with this application (libraries and fonts) are used under their own licenses. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
- The cantus firmi and musical examples included are either in the public domain (such as J. J. Fux, Gradus ad Parnassum, 1725) or were generated by this application. See README.md for details.
